course: dictionary
lesson: 15104
title: Money from other countries
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A rupee is a kind of money. Just as Britain uses pounds and America uses dollars, some countries use rupees to buy things. «My grandma sent me 500 rupees for my birthday.» The word rupees tells you it is money, because a gift of 500 is an amount, and you can buy things with money.
explain: Context helps you find the meaning. «The notebook cost 40 rupees at the shop in Delhi.» Cost tells you the rupees are a price, and a notebook is something you buy. So rupees must be the money used to pay for it. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The notebook cost 40 money» is a little odd, but «40 rupees» tells you how much it costs.
explain: Rupees are used in several countries, including India, Pakistan, Sri Lanka, Nepal and Mauritius. When a text says Indian rupee, it means the rupee used in India. A dictionary or a map can show you which countries use this money.
fact: A rupee is a currency, which means the money a country uses.
fact: Rupee is a noun. You can have one rupee or many rupees.
fact: The rupee is used in India, Pakistan, Sri Lanka, Nepal, Mauritius and other countries.
fact: In India, the symbol for the rupee is ₹.
fact: A phrase you may see is «Indian rupee», which means the rupee of India.
exercise: «The shop sold a pencil for five rupees.» What are rupees here? | Pencils | A kind of fruit | *Money | A school subject
exercise: Which country uses the rupee as its money? | *Nepal | Egypt | Brazil | Japan
exercise: «Mia counted her rupees before she paid.» Find and copy the word that means money. | Mia | counted | paid | *rupees
test: «The Indian rupee is a kind of money.» What does Indian rupee mean? | A kind of hat | A fruit grown in India | *The money of India | A village far away
test: Which symbol shows the rupee in India? | € | *₹ | $ | £
exam: Which sentence uses rupee correctly? | The rupee is my favourite colour. | The river flowed past the hills. | We walked through the rupee in the park. | *The bus ticket cost 10 rupees.
